=== entry e31c37c35e68
kind: translation
rules: model-role, model-effort, general-purpose
intent: Runners come from the `arena runners` line in the project models file, else willyskills's default, one runner per entry, applied with the model-entry snippet (which covers `inherit-parent`). Dropped as Cursor model-catalog rules: the hard-coded default slugs, the rejected-slug fallback with its keep-at-least-two clause, and the family-prefix table (`orchestrator_capabilities` lists what exists). `generalPurpose` is omitted. Preserve the frame steps, the more-runners and repeat-one-model guidance, the poteto-mode effort pointer, and the per-candidate output location.
--- upstream
1. State the artifact each candidate is producing.
2. Derive the rubric, 3-6 concrete gradeable criteria for what success looks like on *this* task. It is the picker's tool in Phase D. Candidates only see the task.
3. Pick the runners from the `arena runners` line in `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, by default `claude-fable-5-2-high`, `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`, and `gemini-4-neon-xhigh`. An `auto` or `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model, so omit `model` and spawn `generalPurpose`. If the Task tool rejects a slug, use the nearest valid slug of the same family or drop the seat, keep at least two runners, and say so. Families go by prefix, and the longest match wins: `claude-fable-*`, `claude-*`, and `gemini-*`, after dropping a leading `cursor-`. Any other slug's family is its text before the first hyphen. Spawn more for multiple design directions, and repeat one model when the work is generation-bound, not judgment-sensitive. Pick each subagent's reasoning level per the Subagents section of the **poteto-mode** skill.
4. Give each candidate its own output location (a git worktree where possible, otherwise `/tmp/arena-<slug>/candidate-<n>/`), per the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill.
--- patched
1. State the artifact each candidate is producing.
2. Derive the rubric, 3-6 concrete gradeable criteria for what success looks like on *this* task. It is the picker's tool in Phase D. Candidates only see the task.
3. Pick the runners from the `arena runners` line in {{snippet:models-file}}, else {{model:arena runners}}, one runner per entry. {{snippet:model-entry}} Spawn more for multiple design directions, and repeat one model when the work is generation-bound, not judgment-sensitive. Pick each subagent's reasoning level per the Subagents section of the **poteto-mode** skill.
4. Give each candidate its own output location (a git worktree where possible, otherwise `/tmp/arena-<slug>/candidate-<n>/`), per the **separate-before-serializing-shared-state** principle skill.

=== entry e0065a2510cb
kind: translation
rules: model-role, same-model-review, delegate, read-only, background
intent: The judge runs on the first entry of the `arena cross-judge pool` line in the project models file, else willyskills's default, as a read-only async `delegate_task` child. Policy (same-model-review): a judge that picks between candidates takes that line as written, so upstream's vendor check (never the parent's vendor, Fable counts as Claude, first entry from another vendor, the unknown-parent case) is dropped rather than translated into a provider comparison; the default pool lists one entry. The nearest-slug and next-entry fallbacks are dropped per model-role, but skipping the judge when the spawn is refused stays, since Phase D and Outputs still allow a skipped judge. Preserve that it starts only after all candidates finish, what it scores, and that it runs while you read in Phase D.
--- upstream
After all Phase B candidates complete, spawn one readonly judge from the `arena cross-judge pool` line in `~/.cursor/rules/pstack-models.mdc`, by default `claude-opus-5-5-high-fast`, `gemini-4-neon-xhigh`. The judge is never from the parent's vendor, and Fable counts as Claude for that check, so use the first entry from another vendor. An `auto` or `inherit-parent` entry is the parent model. If you do not know the parent's model, use the first real slug and say that the vendor check did not run. If the Task tool rejects a slug, use the nearest valid slug of the same family, then the next such entry, or skip the judge, and say so. While you read in Phase D, the judge scores each candidate, by path label, on each rubric criterion and recommends a base.
--- patched
After all Phase B candidates complete, spawn one judge on the first entry of the `arena cross-judge pool` line in {{snippet:models-file}}, else {{model:arena cross-judge pool}}. Spawn it with `delegate_task`, its own `clientRequestId`, `mode: "async"`, and no `isolation`. Keep the returned `taskId` and `childThreadId`. Its brief says "Do not edit, create, commit, or push files.", and you run `git status` afterward. If `delegate_task` rejects that entry, skip the judge and say so. While you read in Phase D, the judge scores each candidate, by path label, on each rubric criterion and recommends a base.
